{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.835323Z","id":"9af25a7800d328f862b2b6ab15b464b9df4a9d480e1aa4459bee94116ed620d2","body":{"detail":"path p export codex|pi|copilot records the caller's cwd (std::env::current_dir) as the session's instead of the source session's; the hermetic tool ran from / and this constant stands in for that. When the export is fixed to carry the source cwd, known_defects@claude.snap changes (written_cwd becomes the source cwd) and this constant becomes unused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"The pipeline hands codex, pi and copilot projectors the hermetic caller cwd `/`, which is what a fixed caller-cwd defect would stop writing","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.846593Z","id":"2a4e07671b0f5bf4860a70cbf11abaa0b0eba48650bdcc83d254467fe141f52d","body":{"detail":"The other three agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, drop the canonical form here so the golden is the real bytes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.856774Z","id":"8cb0124a31291ac6b5706d40348239520356a7341a7ba8604e38ff84b8e6ced9","body":{"detail":"round_trip@copilot@claude.snap is now 'compared' where goldens/roundtrip/copilot-claude.json pinned an error from the hermetic placement step (fixture lacks the session identity claude needs). The Unreadable variant stays for a future pair that genuinely cannot be re-read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"b7b8e0322b119b1e986444e6d40af469ad399cce43b194183a3e3a07d276fb11"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.866880Z","id":"e185bc72fd107804a11a04224fadc4672443192143435772c4cf6f53c3bc8a3a","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. Resolve this record when a defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Three defects pinned as expected current behaviour; a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755754Z","id":"90e64df3125f4d1524949c2e13fb9e19b7c31d40018941fb8df9a61d419d8298","body":{"detail":"path p export codex|pi|copilot records the caller's cwd (std::env::current_dir) as the session's instead of the source session's, and export gemini bakes the caller's directory into projectHash and directories; the hermetic tool ran from / and this constant stands in for that. When the export is fixed to carry the source cwd, known_defects@claude.snap changes (written_cwd becomes the source cwd), every gemini projection's projectHash/directories change, and this constant becomes unused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"The pipeline hands codex, pi, copilot and gemini projectors the hermetic caller cwd `/`, which is what a fixed caller-cwd defect would stop writing","supersedes":"9af25a7800d328f862b2b6ab15b464b9df4a9d480e1aa4459bee94116ed620d2","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755856Z","id":"8d60a30c9a0aba4773d9ea2f561da147417de6323537a02d8275de9cd848c920","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"2a4e07671b0f5bf4860a70cbf11abaa0b0eba48650bdcc83d254467fe141f52d","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755920Z","id":"207c648136a27f9351d94a4c4db84a28d8b042d46b7662455c404a2467d20101","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":508},"end":{"line":508},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"8cb0124a31291ac6b5706d40348239520356a7341a7ba8604e38ff84b8e6ced9","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755974Z","id":"2ac0a1e747def033b9a72aa0296d25d88184ef7c48ef1f5456f2fedb42f0fa00","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. An accounting defect that goes to an empty mismatches list is fixed: accept the snapshot, delete the Defect, and the invariant in tests/goldens.rs tightens by itself. Resolve this record when every defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Six defects pinned as expected current behaviour (three of them accounting gaps that also exempt their set from the accounting invariant); a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","supersedes":"e185bc72fd107804a11a04224fadc4672443192143435772c4cf6f53c3bc8a3a","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756085Z","id":"0b188981a320abccdc1fe377e1ef33b8719cb53679fb2d9ead78c61dd4b426ed","body":{"detail":"When the adapter learns the stream (header line, message lines with `type`, `$set`-style mutations without), replace this with its reader so `read` for Gemini is the adapter's own path for both shapes. Until then `path p derive gemini` cannot read a session Gemini 0.47 wrote, which the gemini golden proves only in-process.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":295},"content_hash":"c3ff8b01e48dbc692c778663e859492367b6fa47184ea4a7e89130426e557f36"},"summary":"The goldens crate assembles Gemini 0.47's JSONL chat stream itself because toolpath_gemini::ConversationReader reads one JSON document only; this is the third copy of that assembly (toolpath-gemini/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs, path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs)","tags":["goldens","gemini","duplication","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756118Z","id":"9cab016c6cb69f9e3bfbbfd32ae7c6cbb861a2784210064ffb51490828c0b46d","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/validate.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756157Z","id":"550eecc82d68305778af78eee98aca3ea199a33d3a8952113c6bf5c10d380821","body":{"detail":"path-cli's lib.rs declares `mod schema` privately and BUNDLED_KINDS likewise, so the goldens crate includes the kind schema files by relative path. Making the module pub (or moving validation next to toolpath::SCHEMA_JSON) would leave one validator; until then a change to path-cli's validation must be mirrored here or validate@<set> stops meaning `path p validate`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"2e76458dc44fc17b7b7690bd49954bdffe4e8760b1e602e2b68a2b282fa2d752"},"summary":"Reimplements path-cli's private `schema` module (base toolpath.schema.json plus the bundled kind schemas by meta.kind) over the same embedded bytes","tags":["goldens","duplication","schema","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/accounting.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756199Z","id":"18549e27eaac75e08112044300f95ae714dcd48327d0c2821f85050a3bc987cf","body":{"detail":"The fixes live in the adapter crates: toolpath_gemini::provider::sum_usage and toolpath_opencode::provider::accumulate_total must add breakdowns class by class as toolpath_convo::extract does since c65a6b6; copilot needs session-level totals carried into the document (derive writes no total_usage) or per-turn input/cache attribution.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"ede19ac64e35ab5434e8e316e60bc7478b77e2c38087c8628f81be6507ca3da1"},"summary":"The accounting contract holds for claude, claude-session, claude-compacted, codex, pi and cursor and is broken for copilot (session totals only on session.shutdown), gemini and opencode (sum_usage/accumulate_total drop per-turn breakdowns); the three gaps are pinned in defects.rs","tags":["goldens","accounting","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
